      "math_academy_id": "e-10995",
      "problem": "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14251052/assets/83b6ad32ee466751506d54dce1f908b5797f10ff8db29b2e9968b8b98d711fce.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has proportional rows: \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14251052/assets/a70bbfde0be5fc6030881e84375f7cfc8d1d9ea0ea5249888bf8e78f426ab25f.svg)\nAs a result, $|A| = 0.$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a triangular matrix, so \n\n$$\n|B| = (-1) \\cdot 4 \\cdot (-3) = 12 \\neq 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has a zero row: \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14251052/assets/8784740caf0d40195eaca895d1df788fd859eace9742f64e7dd57657bd141f0b.svg)\nAs a result, $|C| = 0.$\n\nTherefore, only $|A|$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$",
